module cacd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The Central District of California's own criminal periods, counted
// under the criminal rules (FRCrimP 45(a) governs "any local rule"). No
// trigger carries a service method: FRCrimP 45(c)'s three added days
// follow the manner of service, which is not modeled here.
//
// Periods that are FRCrimP periods stay in lit/frcrimp: counsel must
// observe FRCrimP 32(f) on objections to the presentence report (L.Cr.R.
// 32-3.2), whose period is not restated.
//
// Periods measured in hours stay in notes: a defendant unable to meet
// bail conditions may apply for review and modification twenty-four hours
// after bail is set (L.Cr.R. 46-2), the earliest time to apply rather
// than a deadline; the United States Attorney reports approval or
// disapproval of a surety's documentation within six (6) office working
// hours (L.Cr.R. 46-3.4), and the court holds a hearing on two (2) hours
// notice (L.Cr.R. 46-3.4.1).
//
// Conditions that are not deadlines from an event stay in notes: a case
// with eight or more defendants, or whose case-in-chief will exceed twelve
// trial days, is "complex" and the government files a Notice of Complex
// Case with the indictment (L.Cr.R. 7-3); notices of related criminal and
// supervised-release cases are filed promptly (L.Cr.R. 7-4, 7-5); a
// minimum custody case (probable range unlikely to exceed 4-10 months,
// defendant detained) gets an expedited presentence report (L.Cr.R.
// 32-3.1); a motion to withdraw is made on written notice "reasonably in
// advance" (L.Cr.R. 44-1); a bond judgment may be rendered summarily on
// ten (10) days notice (L.Cr.R. 46-6), a notice the court gives rather
// than a party's deadline; an exemption from electronic filing must not
// exceed one calendar year (L.Cr.R. 49-1.2(a)(2)). The Local Civil Rules
// govern criminal proceedings where applicable (L.Cr.R. 57-1); their
// periods live in lit/cacd.
//
// The earlier C.D. Cal. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// belong to lit/frcrimp; they are removed here: no reporter text is
// vendored.
/// A motion to suppress is served (C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 12-1.2).
event SuppressionMotionServed()
/// The hearing on a motion to suppress is scheduled (C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R.
/// 12-1.3).
event SuppressionHearingScheduled()
/// The trial is scheduled to commence (C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 16-1, 57-3.3.1).
event TrialScheduled()
/// An assignment of monies deposited with the Court is made (C.D. Cal.
/// L.Cr.R. 46-7).
event DepositAssignmentMade()
/// A settlement conference in a complex case is scheduled (C.D. Cal.
/// L.Cr.R. 57-3.5.2).
event SettlementConferenceScheduled()
/// Counsel requests the defendant's criminal history summary from the
/// Probation Officer (C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 57-3.5.2).
event CriminalHistoryRequested()
/// The settlement conference is held and a settlement is agreed (C.D.
/// Cal. L.Cr.R. 57-3.5.4).
event SettlementConferenceHeld()

/// C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 12-1.2: unless otherwise ordered, the government
/// files a response and any opposing declarations not later than seven
/// (7) days after service of the motion to suppress.
deadline suppression-response: 7.days after SuppressionMotionServed() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 12-1.2"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 12-1.3: a party that does not desire to
/// cross-examine a declarant files and serves a notice to that effect no
/// later than one week before the hearing; otherwise the declarant is made
/// available for cross-examination.
deadline declarant-cross-examination-notice: 7.days before SuppressionHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 12-1.3"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 16-1(1): unless the parties agree or the Court orders
/// otherwise, on a timely FRCrimP 16(a)(1)(G)(i) request the government
/// discloses its case-in-chief expert testimony no later than 30 days
/// before trial.
deadline government-expert-disclosure: 30.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 16-1"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 16-1(2): unless the parties agree or the Court orders
/// otherwise, on a timely FRCrimP 16(b)(1)(C)(i) request the defendant
/// discloses its case-in-chief expert testimony no later than 14 days
/// before trial.
deadline defense-expert-disclosure: 14.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 16-1"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 46-7: no assignment of monies deposited with the
/// Court is recognized unless filed with the Clerk within ten (10) days of
/// its making.
deadline deposit-assignment-filing: 10.days after DepositAssignmentMade() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 46-7"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 57-3.3.1: if the trial judge sets no settlement
/// conference cut-off date, a joint request for a settlement conference
/// may be made up to twenty-one (21) days before the date scheduled for
/// trial, unless the trial judge permits a later request.
deadline settlement-conference-request: 21.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 57-3.3.1"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 57-3.5.2: either counsel may request the defendant's
/// criminal history summary from the Probation Officer at least 10 days
/// before the settlement conference.
deadline criminal-history-request: 10.days before SettlementConferenceScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 57-3.5.2"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 57-3.5.2: on a timely request the Probation Officer,
/// without order of the Court, provides the summary to both counsel
/// within 7 days of the request.
deadline criminal-history-summary: 7.days after CriminalHistoryRequested() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 57-3.5.2"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 57-3.5.4: if a settlement is agreed by both counsel
/// and approved by the defendant, the plea agreement is reduced to
/// writing and executed within three (3) court days from the settlement
/// conference.
deadline settlement-plea-agreement: 3.court_days after SettlementConferenceHeld() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "C.D. Cal. L.Cr.R. 57-3.5.4"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
